    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29546" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυσ-τράπελος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>difficult to deal with</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλέψ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Oss.</u>
					16
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρᾶγμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Henioch.
					4.4
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.419a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀφθαλμία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sor.
					2.15
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of persons,
				<i>intractable, stubborn</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				914
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EE</u>
				1234a5
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λως</span>
			<i>awkwardly, clumsily</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Oec.</u>
				8.16
			</span></i>; <i>with difficulty</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.114
			</span></i>.</div>
